<GuideLayout 
  title="Automated QC Systems: Eliminating Human Error in Large-Scale Activewear Orders" 
  type="QUALITY CONTROL"
  description="The technology behind our zero-defect promise. How automated inspection units protect your brand's reputation."
>
  <h2>Zero-Defect Engineering</h2>
  <p>For high-volume orders, manual inspection alone is insufficient. Fitclo utilizes AI-powered automated QC systems to ensure every garment meets the highest standards of your <strong>Supply Chain Partner</strong>.</p>
  
  <h3>AI Fabric Scanners</h3>
  <p>Before a single stitch is made, our automated scanners inspect the raw fabric for micro-holes, color variance, and weaving defects. This <strong>Inventory Management</strong> step at the material level prevents 90% of finished-goods failures.</p>
  
  <h3>Smart Stitch Monitoring</h3>
  <p>Our latest sewing units are equipped with sensors that detect skipped stitches or thread tension fluctuations in real-time. If the machine deviates from the set parameters, it stops automatically, ensuring that no defective item ever enters the packing line.</p>

  <h3>Transparent Reporting for Global Logistics</h3>
  <p>Before your order leaves for <strong>Global Logistics</strong>, we provide digital QC reports including high-resolution photos and lab test results. This transparency is why the world's leading fitness brands trust Fitclo for their large-scale production.</p>
</GuideLayout>
